---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { getLegalPage, legalHref } from '../../lib/legal';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/seo';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/paths';

const page = getLegalPage('terms-of-use')!;
---

<LegalLayout page={page} intro="Please read these terms before using Digital Catholic.">
	<h2>1. Acceptance of terms</h2>
	<p>
		By accessing or using Digital Catholic (the “Website”), you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do
		not agree, please do not use the Website. These terms should be read together with our
		<a href={legalHref('privacy-policy')}>Privacy Policy</a>,
		<a href={legalHref('disclaimer')}>Religious &amp; Educational Disclaimer</a>,
		<a href={legalHref('copyright')}>Copyright &amp; Intellectual Property Policy</a>, and
		<a href={legalHref('external-links')}>External Links Disclaimer</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>2. Website purpose and permitted usage</h2>
	<p>
		Digital Catholic is a free, static educational and devotional library that presents Catholic teaching,
		Scripture-related resources, prayer, liturgy, and related topics in accessible language. You may:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Browse, read, and privately share links to pages for personal, educational, catechetical, or pastoral use.</li>
		<li>Quote short excerpts with clear attribution to Digital Catholic and the page URL, subject to third-party rights described in the Copyright Policy.</li>
		<li>Use the Website in a manner consistent with applicable law and these terms.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>3. User responsibilities</h2>
	<p>When using the Website, you agree to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Use the content lawfully and respectfully.</li>
		<li>Not misrepresent Digital Catholic as an official Church publication or claim ecclesiastical endorsement that does not exist.</li>
		<li>Check important doctrinal, liturgical, or pastoral matters against authoritative Church sources and competent pastoral guidance.</li>
		<li>Provide accurate information if you contact us, and not submit unlawful, abusive, or infringing material.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>4. Prohibited activities</h2>
	<p>You must not:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Attempt to disrupt, scrape aggressively, overload, or interfere with the Website or its hosting infrastructure.</li>
		<li>Use the Website to distribute malware, phishing content, or other harmful material.</li>
		<li>Reproduce substantial portions of the Website’s original content for commercial publication without permission, except as permitted by law or an applicable licence.</li>
		<li>Remove or obscure copyright, attribution, or licence notices associated with content or images.</li>
		<li>Impersonate the maintainer, claim false affiliation with the Catholic Church, or use the Website to deceive others.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>5. Intellectual property ownership</h2>
	<p>
		Original text, site design, branding, and compilation on Digital Catholic are protected by copyright
		and related rights. Third-party images, Scripture translations, prayers, and Church documents remain
		subject to their own ownership and licences. See the
		<a href={legalHref('copyright')}>Copyright &amp; Intellectual Property Policy</a> for details.
	</p>

	<h2>6. Third-party content and resources</h2>
	<p>
		Some pages summarise, quote, or link to Scripture, Catechism references, historical sources, and other
		materials. Inclusion does not transfer ownership of those materials to Digital Catholic, and accuracy
		should be verified against authoritative editions.
	</p>

	<h2>7. External website links</h2>
	<p>
		The Website may link to official Church websites, GitHub, and other independent resources. Those sites
		are not controlled by Digital Catholic. See the
		<a href={legalHref('external-links')}>External Links Disclaimer</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>8. Website availability and maintenance</h2>
	<p>
		The Website is provided on an “as available” basis. It may be updated, corrected, suspended, or
		withdrawn at any time for maintenance, security, hosting changes, or content review. We do not
		guarantee uninterrupted access or that every page will remain permanently available at the same URL.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
	<p>
		To the fullest extent permitted by law, Digital Catholic and its maintainer are not liable for loss or
		damage arising from your use of, or inability to use, the Website, including reliance on educational or
		devotional content, downtime, or third-party sites.
	</p>
	<p>
		Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts, or modifies any consumer guarantee, right, or remedy that
		cannot be excluded under the Australian Consumer Law or other applicable mandatory law. Where liability
		cannot be excluded but can be limited, liability is limited to re-supply of the relevant services or
		payment of the cost of re-supply, as permitted by law.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Changes to the terms</h2>
	<p>
		We may update these Terms of Use from time to time. The “Last updated” date on this page will change
		when revisions are published. Continued use of the Website after changes are posted constitutes
		acceptance of the updated terms, to the extent permitted by law.
	</p>

	<h2>11. Governing law</h2>
	<p>
		These terms are governed by the laws of Western Australia and the applicable laws of the Commonwealth
		of Australia. Subject to any non-excludable rights you may have, courts in Western Australia will have
		non-exclusive jurisdiction over disputes arising from these terms or your use of the Website.
	</p>

	<h2>12. Contact information</h2>
	<p>
		For questions about these terms, email
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
		or use the <a href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact</a> page. Copyright and correction requests should
		follow the <a href={legalHref('corrections')}>Content Corrections &amp; Copyright Requests</a> procedure.
	</p>
</LegalLayout>
